                        ],
                        "library_pattern": "register_identity() first (when applicable — L0 crates). Then domain-specific free functions ordered by frequency of use. Free functions are the 'convenience layer' — they exist for operations that span types or have no natural type home.",
                        "why_these_constraints": "Same as bare-bone — FreeFunctions are the top-level API not attached to any type. In library form, they're positioned LAST in BODY because type methods (B2-B6) are the primary API. Free functions are supplementary."
