                                "Test helpers complex enough to be their own module — extract to test_utils.rs",
                                "Shared mutable state between tests — use TEST_MUTEX pattern when needed",
                                "Tests with ordering dependencies — tests run in any order",
                                "More than one mod tests block — exactly one, in Cv"
                            ],
                            "library_pattern": "Organize tests by BODY section using comment headers. Each section gets at minimum: (1) happy path test, (2) error path test, (3) edge case test. Identity tests (B1) come first — they verify the file IS what it claims to be. Construction tests (B3) second — they verify types come into existence correctly. Logic tests (B4) third — the bulk of testing.",
                            "why_these_constraints": "Library tests are the proof that the public API works. Organizing by BODY section means test coverage maps 1:1 to implementation. Missing a section header means missing test coverage. The comment headers are both organizational AND a coverage checklist."
                        }
                    },

                    "Ce_Execution": {
                        "position": 2,
                        "tag": "Ce",
                        "status": "REQUIRED (always empty for library)",
                        "inherits_constraints": "bare-bone Ce_Execution content_constraints",
                        "library_difference": "Ce is ALWAYS empty for libraries. Libraries have no entry point — they are used, not run. The section exists as a structural slot with a comment explaining why it's empty.",
                        "content_constraints": {
                            "can_contain": [
                                "// Section header comment: 'Ce — Execution (empty — libraries have no entry point)'",
                                "// Brief explanation: consumers call pub API directly, there is no main()"
                            ],
                            "cannot_contain": [
                                "fn main() — libraries are not executables",
                                "Library initialization code — registration is in BODY B7 FreeFunctions",
                                "Auto-start logic — library consumers decide when to call APIs",
                                "Any executable code — Ce is structurally present but content-empty for libraries"
                            ],
                            "library_pattern": "Section header comment only. Two lines: the header tag and a note explaining that libraries are consumed via pub API, not executed.",
                            "why_these_constraints": "Ce exists as a structural slot — the 4-block system requires it. But libraries have no entry point. An empty Ce is CORRECT for library form, not a gap to fill. The comment documents this as intentional design, not oversight."
